{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 9,
  "title": "Legend of sage Rishyashringa",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga9/balasans9.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga9/balaitrans9.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sumantra, the minister of King Dasharatha, details the importance of Sage Rishyasringa and beseeches the king to invite that sage to preside over the contemplated Vedic ritual, for that Sage's entry into any kingdom is auspicious for that land and people."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे नवमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 9th chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.9.1",
      "label": "1.9.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "एतच्छ्रुत्वा रहः सूतो राजानमिदमब्रवीत् |\nश्रूयतां तत् पुरावृत्तं पुराणे च मया श्रुतम्",
      "iast": "etat śrutvā rahaḥ sūto rājānam idam abravIt |\nśrūyatām tat purā vṛttam purāṇe ca mayā śrutam",
      "translation": "Sumantra, the charioteer and one of the misters of King Dasharatha, having heard all about the king's desire to perform a Vedic ritual, said this in confidence to king, \"oh, king, I will tell an early legend, an early legendary narration that I listened...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "etat shrutvaa suutaH",
          "iast": "etat śrutvā sūtaḥ",
          "devanagari": "एतत् श्रुत्वा सूतः",
          "meaning": "all this, having heard, charioteer, Sumantra",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raajaanam",
          "iast": "rājānam",
          "devanagari": "राजानं",
          "meaning": "to king [Dasharatha]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "rahaH idam abraviit",
          "iast": "rahaḥ idam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "रहः इदं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "in confidence, in this way, said",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shruuyataam tat",
          "iast": "śrūyatām tat",
          "devanagari": "श्रूयतां तत्",
          "meaning": "I will tell, that",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "puraa vR^ittam",
          "iast": "purā vṛttam",
          "devanagari": "पुरा वृत्तं",
          "meaning": "an early, legend",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "puraaNe ca mayaa shrutam",
          "iast": "purāṇe ca mayā śrutam",
          "devanagari": "पुराणे च मया श्रुतं",
          "meaning": "legendary narration, also, by me, listened.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.9.2",
      "label": "1.9.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "ऋत्विग्भिरुपदिष्टोऽयं पुरावृत्तो मया श्रुतः |\nसनत्कुमारो भगवान् पूर्वं कथितवान् कथाम्\nऋषीणां सन्निधौ राजंस्तव पुत्रागमं प्रति |",
      "iast": "ṛtvigbhiḥ upadiṣṭo'yam purā vṛtto mayā śrutaḥ |\nsanatkumāro bhagavān pūrvam kathitavān kathām\nṛṣīṇām sannidhau rājan tava putrāagamam prati |",
      "translation": "\"Oh, king, I have earlier heard of this present advice given to you by Vedic scholars, as godly Sage Sanatkumara has once narrated an account about the arrival of your sons in the presence of other sages, and sage Sanat Kumara said...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raajan",
          "iast": "rājan",
          "devanagari": "राजन्",
          "meaning": "oh King",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
